  "name": "Hudke (Karnali hudko-drum ballads)",
  "family": "global",
  "lineage": "Ballad song-dance of the Karnali region of western Nepal, once widely popular in Jumla and in parts of Kalikot and Mugu. Male singer-dancers play the hudko, a hand-held hourglass drum headed with dried goat skin, while they sing ballads and narrative songs, and they perform with the panche baja band at weddings, bratabandha and other social and cultural celebrations; the form is now described as on the verge of disappearance. The Uttarakhand hudka card stands in for the related hudko.",
